&lt;rohitbm@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322825" owner_email="mussa@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/25/322825/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia13f76cb07ff987a97f4cc6a4a35d78e333d404a" commit="e386d7261c9486fbe4b997f3ac6db9fb525bbf8a" commit_message="Simply and specialize a Cyapa FW updater script  Previously, Cypress touchpads (cyapa) were the only ones still using the old monolithic FW updater script.  This worked since the script supported all of the original touchpad types, but was far more complex and hard to read than need be for just Cypress.  Especially with the common functions developed to support the other updater scripts, it could be done much more simply.  This CL deletes the final vestiges of the old FW updating syle and includes a cyapa-specific FW updater script that matches the others in style now.  BUG=chromium:525136 TEST=tested on a Daisy.  I wrote a script to flash various old versions of the fw and then update from them to see how they react.  All appeared to be handled correctly.  Change-Id: Ia13f76cb07ff987a97f4cc6a4a35d78e333d404a Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322714 Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322714" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" ref="refs/changes/14/322714/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia043a4f230c8d5f657b1e21b27140b3cc29fc6a7" commit="d670588fc72c6a6efb26a5ec8306d69f6ba5639d" commit_message="frecon: move maxfd handling inside _add_fds functions  Each invocation of _add_fds was adding 1 and using calling a function from MAX() macro which could call it more than once.  BUG=none TEST=run frecon on daisy-spring  Change-Id: Ia043a4f230c8d5f657b1e21b27140b3cc29fc6a7 Signed-off-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322768 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="322768" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/frecon" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/frecon" ref="refs/changes/68/322768/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I541d50e1dfe61c13ffc5ee76024d07bb41e7b5bd" commit="612e7ae643617be04d8183be0a1787ddc018bfaf" commit_message="LKGMManager: Patch manifest changes before creating test manifest.  Patch the repo manifests with any changes for manifest-internal, and include those changes in the versioned manifest used by the CQ slave builders.  BUG=chromium:549844 TEST=cbuildbot/run_tests      cbuildbot --buildbot --debug --local -g 319141 --bootstrap-args      '-g *242726' --test-bootstrap --buildroot &lt;tmpdir&gt; mixed-a-pre-cq  Change-Id: I541d50e1dfe61c13ffc5ee76024d07bb41e7b5bd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/319141 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David James &lt;davidjames@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="319141" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/41/319141/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="7852.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>